## 3. Step-by-Step Lab Workflow

| Step | Stage | What Happens | Main Role |
| ---- | ----- | ------------ | --------- |
| 1 | Order received | Order appears on lab workbench from OPD/IPD/ICU/clinical. | System |
| 2 | Billing gate (if required) | Pay-now or bill-later at order time. | Cashier / System |
| 3 | Sample collection | Collect, label, send to lab. | Phlebotomist / Lab |
| 4 | Sample receive / reject | Accession or reject with reason. | Lab tech |
| 5 | Processing | Test in progress. | Lab tech |
| 6 | Result entry | Enter values; flag critical results. | Lab tech |
| 7 | Verification | Verify/release or reject result. | Lab supervisor |
| 8 | Clinician notification | Critical results notify doctor/ward ([ipd-flow Â§17](./ipd-flow.mdc)). | System |

---

## 4. Backend Workbench Contract

Use `GET /lab/workbench` and lab-workspace workflow mutations as canonical. Order pipeline: collect â' receive/reject sample â' release/reject result â' verify â' reverse (when permitted).

| Order status (user meaning) | Lab action |
| --------------------------- | ---------- |
| Ordered | Awaiting sample |
| Waiting sample / patient | Collect sample |
| In progress | Processing |
| Result pending | Entry in progress |
| Completed | Released to clinician |
| Cancelled | Cancel with reason |

